From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 11:57:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-wahoo: fix duplicate
 panel-ldo node name

The two fixed regulators for the panel shared the node name
"panel-ldo", so dtc silently merged them: the built DTB carried a
single node whose properties came from whichever definition parsed
last, panel_ldo_vddio_supply and panel_ldo_vpnl_supply were two labels
on that one node, and the vddio GPIO (tlmm 133) was never driven.
Give each regulator its own node name.

Also reword a comment that contained "drivers/net/ipa/*", which forms
'/*' inside a block comment and made dtc warn on every build.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
index 388781562490..8e29213fc6c0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ vph_pwr: vph-pwr-regulator {
 		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
-	panel_ldo_vddio_supply: panel-ldo {
+	panel_ldo_vddio_supply: panel-ldo-vddio {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "panel_ldo_vddio_supply";
 
@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@ panel_ldo_vddio_supply: panel-ldo {
 		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
-	panel_ldo_vpnl_supply: panel-ldo {
+	panel_ldo_vpnl_supply: panel-ldo-vpnl {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "panel_ldo_vpnl_supply";
 
@@ -610,8 +610,9 @@ &ufsphy {
  * WLAN-datapath rationale) has no base node to attach to: 6.18's
  * msm8998.dtsi carries no top-level "ipa" node at all yet, unlike our
  * 6.0 base. Needs the ipa SoC node ported into msm8998.dtsi first
- * (drivers/net/ipa/* is also unported -- gsi.c, ipa_gsi.c, ipa_modem.c
- * are all in the milestone-2 list), then this override can come back.
+ * (the drivers/net/ipa code is also unported -- gsi.c, ipa_gsi.c,
+ * ipa_modem.c are all in the milestone-2 list), then this override can
+ * come back.
  */
 
 &wifi {
